                                    </div>

                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>Do consumers actually pay more for sustainable products?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes, but the premium varies: 5-10% in India, 15-30% in USA / UK / Australia. Premium requires credibility — vague claims see no premium.</p>
                                        <h3>Is B Corp certification worth the effort?</h3>
                                        <p>For most brands, yes. It's the most credible general sustainability certification and directly lifts CVR 5-12% in receptive markets. Timeline: 6-14 months. Cost: $3K-40K.</p>
                                        <h3>What is the biggest greenwashing mistake?</h3>
                                        <p>Sustainability-only positioning without measurement or certification. Customers assume you're hiding poor practices. Lead with product benefit; back sustainability with data.</p>
                                        <h3>Should packaging be compostable or recyclable?</h3>
                                        <p>Depends on regional infrastructure. Recyclable is safer in most markets. Compostable only works if you can guide customers to industrial composting; home composting rarely handles most 'compostable' materials.</p>
